Subject: HWUI: recover from a GPU device loss and draw every window again

HWUI aborted when the GPU device was lost: "Lost GPU device unexpectedly" at the start of a
frame, "Encountered EGL error 12302 EGL_CONTEXT_LOST during rendering" in eglSwapBuffers, and
Skia's Vulkan device lost callback.

RenderThread now finds the loss (the EGL display answers EGL_CONTEXT_LOST, or Skia abandoned
its context), abandons the GrDirectContext, destroys the EGL or Vulkan context and every
window's surface, and builds them again once the host GPU answers, trying with backoff without
blocking the thread. Each window then draws again in full from its display lists, and the
next sync asks the UI thread to draw it again (SyncResult::UIRedrawRequired). A process also
rebuilds when SurfaceFlinger reports a reset through debug.dsa.gpu.resets, so idle windows are
drawn again too. Paths that need a context (layers, TextureView frames, readback, hardware
bitmap uploads) wait or fail softly while there is none.

Applies to frameworks/base at 94b4c163b7dfe5ce3607f7bb8456f9573f7de57d (Android 17).
